WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:03.169 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i>[soft piano music]</i>

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.004 align:start size:81% position:19%
(Narrator)
Since ancient times,

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.716 align:start size:81% position:19%
we have sought to
know the human mind.

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:12.429 align:start size:81% position:19%
The first scientists
and philosophers

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:15.473
asked some of the same
questions we pose today.

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:19.269 line:0%
<i>[strings join in music]</i>

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:19.269
What do we see, and why?

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.688
How do we learn,

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.274
and why do we forget?

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:27.402
Where do ideas come from,

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:30.113 align:start size:78% position:22%
and how do we
generate knowledge?

00:00:31.781 --> 00:00:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
Human cognition is the basis
for our accomplishments,

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.913 align:start size:59% position:41% line:0%
[audience cheering]

00:00:38.913 --> 00:00:42.709
yet understanding it
has proven elusive.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.503
Learning more about
how we perceive,

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:46.796
how we think,

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:49.466
and how we engage with others

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:53.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
is one of the most important
endeavors of our time.

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:56.639 line:71%
<i>[music builds]</i>

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:56.639
Yale can take us there.

00:00:56.639 --> 00:01:00.351
The vision - a bold union
of scientific approaches

00:01:00.351 --> 00:01:03.354 align:start size:91% position:9%
that lead to us to an
understanding of cognition.

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:05.815 align:start size:84% position:16%
Beginning with the
basic building blocks.

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:09.194
Genes, molecules, and cells.

00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:13.031
Mental processes that
build to behavior.

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:15.200
Algorithms that lend insight

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.535 align:start size:84% position:16%
into the inner
workings of the brain.

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:20.205
Combine these components
with the diverse community

00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:23.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
of scientists and scientific
interests at Yale,

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.294 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we can reveal the
capabilities of the mind.

00:01:26.294 --> 00:01:31.382 align:start size:97% position:3%
We will understand how our
brains grow, change, and rewire

00:01:31.382 --> 00:01:34.093 align:start size:88% position:13%
with the goal of
preserving and enhancing

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:37.263 align:start size:91% position:9%
the remarkable flexibility
of the human brain.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:41.100 align:start size:91% position:9%
We will describe brain
function with new precision

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.562 align:start size:97% position:3%
using computational approaches
to map the contours of

00:01:44.562 --> 00:01:47.482 align:start size:84% position:16%
perception, reasoning,
and memory.

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:51.569
We will marry disparate data
types to model human cognition

00:01:51.569 --> 00:01:53.863 align:start size:81% position:19%
and advance
machine intelligence.

00:01:54.697 --> 00:01:57.200
To discover deeper truths,

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.118
learn in new ways,

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:01.830
and teach a new generation.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:06.209 align:start size:91% position:9%
The future of neuroscience
begins here.

00:02:06.835 --> 00:02:09.254
To know, together.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:13.967 align:start size:6% position:94% line:0%
<i>♪♪</i>

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:13.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is the Wu Tsai Institute
at Yale University.

